select: select

Each case of a select becomes an object, made in source order before the select runs:
gp::sel_send(ch, v), gp::sel_recv(ch, ...) or gp::sel_default. The channel and the value of
each case are evaluated once, in Go's order (a call in a later case cannot change an earlier
channel). gp::select(cases...) waits until a case can proceed, picks one of the ready ones
at random as Go does, and returns its index; a C++ switch on the index runs the case's body.
The variables that a receive case declares are assigned in the first statement of the case.

break leaves the C++ switch, like Go's select; continue and labelled jumps belong to the
enclosing loop. A select without cases blocks the goroutine forever (gp::select()). A select
with a default never blocks.

Specification: docs/spec/cpp-mapping.md#goroutines-and-channels
See also: gocpp explain channels, gocpp explain goroutines
Also known as: selects

Example (select.gp):

    package main

    import "fmt"

    func main() {
    	a, b := make(chan int, 1), make(chan string, 1)
    	a <- 1
    	select {
    	case v := <-a:
    		fmt.Println("a", v)
    	case s := <-b:
    		fmt.Println("b", s)
    	default:
    		fmt.Println("none")
    	}
    }

The C++ that gocpp emit -annotate writes for it:

    //// gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp
    // gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp: generated by gocpp, do not edit
    #pragma once
    #include <gocpp/rt.hpp>

    namespace gpkg_main {
    void main();

    } // namespace gpkg_main
    //// gpkg/command-line-arguments/select.gp.cpp
    // gpkg/command-line-arguments/select.gp.cpp: generated by gocpp, do not edit
    #include "gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp"

    namespace gpkg_main {

    // ---- ./select.gp:5: func main() {
    void main() {

    // ---- ./select.gp:6: a, b := make(chan int, 1), make(chan string, 1)
    // gp[channels] col 10: make(chan): allocates the channel; a gp::chan is a shared reference, so
    //     copies and directional views share one channel
    // gp[channels] col 29: make(chan): allocates the channel; a gp::chan is a shared reference, so
    //     copies and directional views share one channel
        gp::chan<int64_t> a = gp::make_chan<int64_t>(1);
        gp::chan<gp::string> b = gp::make_chan<gp::string>(1);

    // ---- ./select.gp:7: a <- 1
    // gp[channels] col 2: send: blocks until a receiver is ready or the buffer has room; sending on a
    //     closed channel panics, on a nil channel blocks forever
        gp::send(a, 1);

    // ---- ./select.gp:8: select {
    // gp[select] col 2: select with 3 cases: each case becomes an object (gp::sel_send, gp::sel_recv,
    //     gp::sel_default) made in source order; gp::select picks one ready case at random (or waits)
    //     and the C++ switch runs its body
        {

    // ---- ./select.gp:9: case v := <-a:
            gp::sel_recv gp_s0{a};

    // ---- ./select.gp:11: case s := <-b:
            gp::sel_recv gp_s1{b};

    // ---- ./select.gp:8: select {  (continued)
            switch (gp::select(gp_s0, gp_s1, gp::sel_default)) {

    // ---- ./select.gp:9: case v := <-a:  (continued)
            case 0: {
                int64_t v = gp_s0.gp_take();

    // ---- ./select.gp:10: fmt.Println("a", v)
    // gp[interfaces] col 3: fmt.Println: the runtime's gp::fmt functions take each operand with the
    //     descriptor of its Go type (gp::fmt::as), not boxed into an interface first (an operand of a
    //     non-pointer type with an Error method is, see the allocation note)
                gp::fmt::Println("a"_gs, v);
            } break;

    // ---- ./select.gp:11: case s := <-b:  (continued)
            case 1: {
                gp::string s = gp_s1.gp_take();

    // ---- ./select.gp:12: fmt.Println("b", s)
                gp::fmt::Println("b"_gs, s);
            } break;

    // ---- ./select.gp:13: default:
            default: {

    // ---- ./select.gp:14: fmt.Println("none")
                gp::fmt::Println("none"_gs);
            } break;

    // ---- ./select.gp:15: }
            }
        }

    // ---- ./select.gp:16: }
    }

    } // namespace gpkg_main
